* Channels

Channels are a typed conduit through which you can send and receive values with the channel operator, ⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000001⟫<-⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000002⟫.

⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000003⟫Send ⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000004⟫ to channel ⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000005⟫.⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000006⟫Receive from ⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000007⟫, and⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000008⟫assign value to ⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000009⟫.⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000010⟫(The data flows in the direction of the arrow.)

Like maps and slices, channels must be created before use:

⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000011⟫

By default, sends and receives block until the other side is ready. This allows goroutines to synchronize without explicit locks or condition variables.

The example code sums the numbers in a slice, distributing the work between two goroutines.
Once both goroutines have completed their computation, it calculates the final result.

⟪GTI18N_a35e3af2_000012⟫

